    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm currently reviewing the Q3 expense reports for our manufacturing plant and noticed some oddities in the miscellaneous office supplies ledger. There are these small, recurring discrepancies—nothing huge, maybe just a few dozen euros here and there—but they don't follow any specific pattern and they keep popping up in different sub-accounts. I want to look into this more closely without triggered a full, formal forensic audit yet. Can you suggest a systematic way to investigate these small irregularities to see if there's a pattern or if it's just clerical error?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
