      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A systematic approach for these small, recurring discrepancies is a good idea before escalating to a full audit. You could start by grouping the transactions by vendor, date range, and the specific sub-account where they appear. This initial triage will help you see if a particular vendor or a specific time period is the source of the 'oddities.' If you find a cluster, you can then drill down into the supporting documentation for those specific entries. This targeted approach is much less invasive than a full forensic dive, which is what you're aiming for right now.",
