      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since vendor grouping didn't yield results, you need to look at the *context* of the expense, not just the amount or the supplier. Cross-referencing the expense dates against employee activity logs or shift schedules might reveal a pattern related to who was working or what tasks were being performed that week. Furthermore, look at the *time* the expense was recorded in the system versus when the receipt was supposedly generated, which can sometimes point to clerical lag or deliberate manipulation. This helps distinguish between a simple data entry error and something more deliberate.",
