      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the amounts are so small, you need to implement a threshold-based anomaly detection, which is a much smarter way to hunt these slippages. Instead of flagging *every* small transaction, set a dynamic threshold—perhaps anything that is less than a certain amount *and* occurs outside of normal business hours, or any transaction that repeats within a short window across different accounts. This allows you to isolate the \"petty\" noise without drowning in the legitimate, tiny purchases. You are essentially looking for the *pattern of insignificance*.",
